WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.301
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.769
welcome to "the Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.704
Thank you for being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:14.680 line:0%
-Happy Monday.
Today is Cyber Monday.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.083
Yeah.
I love shopping on Cyber Monday,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.185
'cause nothing beats spending
the holiday season

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.554
on hold with the Bank of America
fraud department.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.223
[ Laughter ]
"Huh?

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.159
No, I didn't buy a TV from
Walmart in the Philippines.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.895
No, that wasn't me."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.731
Yep, over 60 million people
bought gifts today,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.367
yet somehow, on Christmas, all
we do is exchange gift cards.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:38.070
How does that work?
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.740
But it was a big day.
Amazon offered tons of deals,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.775
Target rolled out
major discounts,

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:45.378
and RadioShack was like, "We
should really get a website."

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.846
[ Laughter ]
"We should do that.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.114
Maybe next year.
Make a note."

00:00:49.114 --> 00:00:50.983
Yep, most people
prefer online shopping

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:53.253
because it's easier
and because we're tired of

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:56.355
having to sadly raise our hand
at the self-checkout machines.

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:57.723
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.723 --> 00:00:59.926
"I'm an adult who needs help.
Thanks."

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.894
[ Laughter ]
"Do I weigh my bag,

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.096
or give me the bag, and --

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:05.631
Just give me --
I'll buy two bags.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.767
What is --"
[ Applause ]

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.236
"How did it know that I didn't
put the thing in the bag."

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.971
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.007
What's going on?
Meanwhile, today, in Washington,

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:16.975
First Lady Jill Biden revealed
this year's

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:18.944
White House holiday decorations.

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:23.916
There are 41 Christmas trees
and almost 80,000 lights.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.919
Meanwhile, the family
at 1602 Pennsylvania Avenue

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.822
is like, "They always
have to one-up us every year.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.324
They gotta one-up."

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.992
The theme
of this year's decorations

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.895
is Gifts from the Heart.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.096
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.765
As opposed to today's theme,

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.066
Gifts I Found Online
for 60% Off.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:42.301
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:43.669
Kinda from the heart, yeah.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:46.139
Yet there are 41 Christmas trees
in the White House,

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.040
and even former President Trump

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.475
made it onto
one of the ornaments.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.210
This is real.
This is a real ornament.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.745
Take a look at this.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.879
You see him?
There he is.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.915
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.716
You know that's definitely
on the side of the tree

00:01:57.716 --> 00:02:01.954
that faces the wall, you know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.523
"You made that yourself?
Let me hang it up."

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:06.659
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.560
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
amazing, amazing.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.995
It looks like a reindeer.

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:11.997
It looks just like you made a
reindeer out of pop sticks.

00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:14.700
There you go, back there.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.135
'Course, the big news
that everyone is talking about

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:19.805 line:0%
is this new COVID variant,
called omicron.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.573 line:0%
Yeah, we need another variant

00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:23.476
like we another
turkey sandwich for lunch.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.643
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:25.945
Omicron.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.247
It sounds like a Transformer
who can't smell or taste.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:31.284
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:35.955
"Omicron!"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.258
We're getting kind of deep
in the Greek alphabet, you know?

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:40.693
Pretty soon, we're gonna
run out of letters

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.496
and just start using Gatorade
flavors, you know?

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.765
Fauci will be like,
"We have to do whatever it takes

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.100
to stop
the fierce melon variant."

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.036
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.538
Yeah, basically,
everyone is bummed out

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:53.706
about the new variant.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.442
Meanwhile, Delta Airlines
is like, "Oh, yeah!

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.544
Hey-ya!
What's up?!

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.179
I knew we were gonna --
Come on!"

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:02.315
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.717
But the White House
is trying to handle it today.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.685
President Biden
held a press conference,

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:08.420
and he told Americans
that the new variant

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.158 line:0%
is a cause for concern,
not a cause for panic.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.193
Americans heard and were like,
"Well, in that case,

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.695
we'll just buy 10 pallets of
toilet paper instead of 12."

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:18.998
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.699
But the White House said
it will take two weeks

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:23.302
to have definitive data
on the new strain.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.205
That's right, even our COVID
information has shipping delays.

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.641
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.043
Unbelievable.

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:35.648
[ Applause ]
Of course -- [ Chuckles ]

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.317
Of course, Biden told everyone
to get their booster.

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:39.786
And he said
to carve out some time,

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.889
because rolling up your sleeves
takes longer than you think.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.598
-Is the First Lady getting one,
as well, Mr. President?

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.767
-She's gonna get one.
I think she's teaching.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:58.237
But she's gonna get one, yes.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.973
-Mr. President
what do you say...

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:04.777
-What in the world?!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.278
Oh, my God.

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.981
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:10.616
Oh, my gosh.
At that point,

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:13.185
Just take your shirt off.
What are we --

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.487
What is going on?
[ Applause ]

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:18.123
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.125
Never seen anything like it.

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:21.627
Some major business news.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:25.631 line:0%
Today, Jack Dorsey stepped down
as the CEO of Twitter.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.466
[ Scattered cheers ]
Yep.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.168
Twitter hopes
that his replacement can find

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.236
new and exciting ways
for strangers

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:32.705
to say horrible things
to each other.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.407
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.142
I think Dorsey
made the right decision, though.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.910
It seems like the job
really took a toll on him.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.213
Here he is nine years ago.
That's him.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:43.282
And here he is today.
This is real.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:46.619
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.288
Even Obama's like,
"Man, that job really aged you."

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:52.991
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:56.529
That's real.
I mean...

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.932
It's definitely a sign to leave
your job when you're 45

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.034
and you look like Tom Hanks
at the end of "Castaway."

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.536
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:07.239
Some news from overseas.
Apparently, Kim Jong-un

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:10.309
banned leather coats
in North Korea

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.644
so that nobody
can copy his style.

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:14.146
[ Laughter ]
This is real.

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:16.415
Can we see him
in his leather jacket?

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:18.116
-Yeah.
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:18.116 --> 00:05:20.486
Right now, there's a giant
police raid in the sofa section

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.654
at Raymour &amp; Flanigan.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.589
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.824
Well, get this -- due to
a huge snowstorm in the U.K.,

00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:29.494 line:0%
more than 60 people, including
members of an Oasis cover band,

00:05:29.494 --> 00:05:32.598 line:0%
have been stuck in a pub
since Friday night.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.666
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.067
Yeah.
After three days,

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.635
everyone was fighting
with each other.

00:05:36.635 --> 00:05:38.871
It was almost like
they were in the band Oasis.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.505
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.505 --> 00:05:42.875
Almost.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.243
And finally,
this is going viral.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.712
Someone filmed a fellow driver
on the highway

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.581
with a Christmas tree
that might have been

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:50.082
just a bit too big
for their car.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.183
Take a look at this.

00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.351 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.987
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.987 --> 00:06:00.226 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.994
-He was like,
"This is gonna look great

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.229
in my studio apartment."

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:05.464
Well, guys, Pfizer and Moderna
both say

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.566 line:0%
that they're already working
on vaccines

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.935 line:0%
for the Omicron variant.

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:12.938
While Johnson &amp; Johnson
is cheering them on.

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:15.007
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:21.214
Yeah, Johnson &amp; Johnson is like,
"Guys, I thought we promised

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.848
we're not doing vaccines
this year.

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:25.484
[ Laughter ]
Why would you embarrass me?"

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.219
How'd they start working on this
so fast, too?

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:28.887
It's like when a team
wins the Super Bowl

00:06:28.887 --> 00:06:30.256
and the first commercial is,
"Buy your

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:31.891
Buccaneers Championship
hat now!"

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.026
[ Laughter ]
You're like, "Wait."

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.227
Meanwhile, officials
just announced

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:39.265
that Omicron was present
in Amsterdam 11 days ago.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:40.833
[ Audience oohs ]

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.935
It took a while to catch it
because, in Amsterdam,

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.470
there's a very different meaning
to "a new strain going around."

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:47.506
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:50.376
[ Clears throat ]

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.677
Yeah.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.012
Certain sections of our audience
got that faster

00:06:54.012 --> 00:06:56.148
[ Laughter and applause ]
than others.

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:58.551
Yeah, following the news
on the Omicron variant,

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.853 line:0%
the CDC is now saying
that all adults

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:03.255 line:0%
should get a booster shot.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:04.590 line:0%
Right now, Instagram is like,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.759
"Incoming booster selfies
in 3, 2, 1!"

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.027
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.027 --> 00:07:10.630
Well, guys,
tomorrow's December 1st

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.464
and everyone's starting
to decorate for the holidays,

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:14.699 line:0%
so, the FAA
is warning people not

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:16.601 line:0%
to shine laser light displays

00:07:16.601 --> 00:07:18.770 line:0%
into the sky.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.406
The pilots are actually fine
with the lasers.

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:23.075
It's the emotional support cats
onboard that go nuts.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:24.676
[ Laughter ]
They're just like --

00:07:24.676 --> 00:07:26.345
[ Applause ]

00:07:31.416 --> 00:07:33.352
Well, this is cool --
Roomba updated

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:36.588
its latest vacuum cleaner
so that they use AI

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:38.591
to avoid knocking over
Christmas trees.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:40.959
[ Laughter ]
But don't worry --
with the new update,

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:43.061
your Roombas will still inhale
the tree skirt,

00:07:43.061 --> 00:07:44.730
until it blows up
and burns your house down.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.798
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:48.300
It was kind of weird
when the Roomba

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.002
kept knocking over the
Christmas tree and then going --

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.170
[ Robotic voice ]
Hanukkah rules.

00:07:51.236 --> 00:07:52.104
Hanukkah rules.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.606
Hanukkah rules.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:56.341
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.341 --> 00:07:58.878 line:0%
Hey, I saw that a new study said
that babies start to develop

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:02.013 line:0%
a sense of humor
after one month.

00:08:02.013 --> 00:08:03.449
It's pretty obvious
when your baby's like --

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:04.850
[ As Jerry Seinfeld ]
What's the deal with naps?

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.418
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:08.054
What am I so tired from?

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:10.055
All I did before this
was sleep!

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:11.623
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:14.493
Soft foods, wearing diapers,
napping before sleep --

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:15.861
I'm turning into Grandpa!

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:20.233
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:21.467
I wrote a full-on Seinfeld
-Wow.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:22.901
Fantastic.
-stand-up act as a baby, yeah.

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:24.503
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:26.505
Get this -- I read that,
this year, in America,

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:30.409 line:0%
210 million packages
have already been stolen.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.078
[ Audience oohs ]

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:33.545
Yeah, it turns out
those Ring doorbells

00:08:33.545 --> 00:08:34.647
were a lot more effective

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:36.315
before everyone started
wearing masks.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.850
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "Uh, yes,

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:39.952
two humans?
I don't know.

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:41.888
Does that help you, Officer?

00:08:41.888 --> 00:08:44.589
It wasn't a coyote that took
the package, yeah."

00:08:44.589 --> 00:08:47.826
[ Laughter ]
Finally, police in Germany
are looking for burglars

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:50.061 line:0%
who broke through the wall
of a toy store

00:08:50.061 --> 00:08:52.765 line:0%
to steal dozens of LEGO sets.

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.299
The store was like,
"Ah, maybe we shouldn't have

00:08:54.299 --> 00:08:55.701
built that wall with DUPLOs."

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.837
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.639 --> 00:09:02.608
The thieves got away,
but said their one regret was

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.544
robbing the place barefoot.
Ow!

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:10.382
Well, guys tonight was
the 89th annual

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:12.651
Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree lighting.

00:09:12.651 --> 00:09:14.687
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:18.457
It is the most beautiful thing
you can see in Rockefeller Plaza

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.258
besides ice skaters
falling down.

00:09:20.258 --> 00:09:21.560
It really is. I think so.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.896
Having a giant tree outside
is great, though.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:25.330
It is that special time of year

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.799
when Rockefeller Center smells
like the inside of an Uber.

00:09:27.799 --> 00:09:29.368
Don't you think?
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.937
The tree really is
a sight to behold, though.

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:34.406
It's decorated with
more than 50,000 lights.

00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:35.974
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:37.642
Then, one guy
plugged in his Tesla

00:09:37.642 --> 00:09:39.244
and the whole city blacked out.
-Oh.

00:09:39.244 --> 00:09:41.347
[ Laughter ]
-"Got to charge it up, dude!"

00:09:41.347 --> 00:09:43.649
[ Laughter ]
If that's not enough,

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:46.986
the tree is topped with a star
covered in 3 million crystals.

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:50.055
And one construction worker
they forgot to bring down.

00:09:50.055 --> 00:09:52.157
"Help! Hey!"
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:54.527
Yep, thousands of people
were in attendance.

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:56.194
Thousands of people.
Even the tree was like,

00:09:56.194 --> 00:09:57.796
"Um, can everyone
just throw on a mask

00:09:57.796 --> 00:10:00.699
and take like six steps back,
please?"

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.402
People were waiting outside
for the tree lighting all day.

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.070
After a few hours,
one guy was like,

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.872
"I can't remember
which is my pee bottle

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.374
and which is
my hot cider bottle."

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:11.410
[ Audience groans ]
"It happens everybody year!"

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.978
[ Rim shot ]
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.978 --> 00:10:15.414
"I got to get a label maker
next year."

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:16.582
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:18.650
"I got to charge my Tesla."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:21.453
Meanwhile, earlier,
in the White House,

00:10:21.453 --> 00:10:23.421
on the fourth night of Hanukkah,

00:10:23.421 --> 00:10:25.558 line:53%
President Biden
hosted a menorah lighting.

00:10:25.558 --> 00:10:28.327 line:53%
Nothing says you really care
about a holiday

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:30.095
like waiting until the
fourth night to celebrate.

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:33.999
That's what I...
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:37.202
There was a fun moment tonight
when Biden looked at the menorah

00:10:37.202 --> 00:10:39.638
and said, "When I was a kid,
we called this a flashlight."

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:42.908
[ Laughter ]

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:47.413 line:53%
Some more news -- an FDA panel
just voted 13-10

00:10:47.413 --> 00:10:51.850 line:53%
to narrowly endorse Merck's
anti-viral COVID pill.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.652
Yeah, when it comes
to medication,

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:56.655
I'm not sure "narrowly endorsed"
is the phrase you want to hear.

00:10:56.655 --> 00:10:58.123
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.123 --> 00:11:00.759
The drug, they said,
is only 30% effective.

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:02.627
[ Laughter ]

00:11:02.627 --> 00:11:05.964
For context, that's only 30%
more effective than a calzone.

00:11:05.964 --> 00:11:08.967
Just putting it in context.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.967 --> 00:11:11.704 line:53%
Some political news --
Dr. Oz officially announced

00:11:11.704 --> 00:11:14.840 line:60%
that he is running for
U.S. Senate in Pennsylvania.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.375
Yeah, he's diving right in.

00:11:16.375 --> 00:11:18.376
And he's even testing out
some campaign slogans

00:11:18.376 --> 00:11:20.780
to see what people respond to.
-Really?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.281
-Yep, check some of these out.
First up, there's,

00:11:22.281 --> 00:11:25.151 line:0%
"Dr. Oz -- make America turn
their head and cough again."

00:11:25.151 --> 00:11:26.886 line:0%
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.886 --> 00:11:29.354 line:0%
-Next, there's "Dr. Oz --
stick around after the break.

00:11:29.354 --> 00:11:31.256 line:0%
I'm talking to people
who can't sneeze."

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:35.127 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:36.695 line:0%
-What?!
-Yeah, that's an episode.

00:11:36.695 --> 00:11:39.197 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
-He's also trying out,

00:11:39.197 --> 00:11:41.132 line:0%
"Dr. Oz, just call me
'Dr. Philly!'

00:11:41.132 --> 00:11:44.236 line:0%
Wait, that doesn't work."
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.236 --> 00:11:46.505 line:0%
Up next, there's,
"Dr. Oz -- I know Oprah."

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:47.839 line:0%
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:50.709 line:0%
Followed by, "Dr. Oz --
no, really, I know her."

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:52.778 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
And finally, "Dr. Oz --

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:54.413 line:0%
I mean, we haven't really
spoken recently,

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:56.681 line:0%
but she gives my texts
a 'thumbs up' sometimes."

00:11:56.681 --> 00:11:58.284 line:0%
Fast one.
[ Applause ]

00:11:58.284 --> 00:12:01.553
[ Chuckling ]

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.388
Uh, hey, did you guys
hear about this?

00:12:03.388 --> 00:12:05.824 line:0%
CNN has suspended Chris Cuomo
indefinitely

00:12:05.824 --> 00:12:08.460 line:0%
for his role in advising
his brother Andrew Cuomo

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.262 line:0%
during his recent scandal.

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:12.397
[ Audience oohs ]
Yeah.

00:12:12.397 --> 00:12:13.798
Chris Cuomo
knew something was up

00:12:13.798 --> 00:12:16.468
when CNN added a suspension
countdown clock.

00:12:16.468 --> 00:12:19.471
Yeah, you could tell
Cuomo really misses CNN.

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:21.173
Today he walked up
to a pair of strangers

00:12:21.173 --> 00:12:22.440
and asked if he could stand
between them

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:23.609
while they yell at each other.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:24.109
-Oh, my gosh.

00:12:24.476 --> 00:12:25.710
This is exciting, actually.
Get this.

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:29.648
Walmart -- love Walmart --
Walmart is selling a baking kit

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:33.252 line:53%
with everything you need to make
a family-sized Twinkie.

00:12:33.252 --> 00:12:34.587 line:57%
[ Cheers ]

00:12:35.587 --> 00:12:38.156
Move over, Pfizer and Moderna.

00:12:38.156 --> 00:12:40.793
We got a new favorite for
the Nobel Prize right here!

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.894
Family-size Twinkie!

00:12:42.894 --> 00:12:45.263
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:45.263 --> 00:12:46.699
Seriously, where was this kit

00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:48.834
when we were all buying
sourdough starters?

00:12:48.834 --> 00:12:51.236
I mean, come on.
The great thing about Twinkies

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:53.805
is that you can serve it as a
Christmas dessert this year.

00:12:53.805 --> 00:12:56.007
And if you don't finish it,
it'll be fresh for next year.

00:12:56.007 --> 00:12:57.676
[ Laughter ]

00:12:57.676 --> 00:13:00.012 line:8%
And finally, I saw that Cardi B
is launching

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:02.748 line:8%
her own line of vodka-infused
whipped cream.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:03.849 line:0%
[ Audience groans ]

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:06.117
Thank God.
Something to help me forget

00:13:06.117 --> 00:13:08.387
I just sprayed an entire can
of whipped cream in my mouth.

00:13:08.387 --> 00:13:09.721
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.721 --> 00:13:11.056
Higgins you can bring it --
-I know,

00:13:11.056 --> 00:13:12.757
I should have brought it
to the nativity scene.

00:13:12.757 --> 00:13:15.027
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God, Cardi.

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:18.397
-Luckily, it's non-dairy
for all the health-conscious

00:13:18.397 --> 00:13:20.732
vodka-infused whipped-cream
eaters out there.

00:13:20.732 --> 00:13:22.768
But this is great.
You squirt a little of that

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:24.770
inside a family-size Twinkie,
now, that's a party.

00:13:25.904 --> 00:13:28.373
in Washington, D.C.,

00:13:28.373 --> 00:13:29.808 line:0%
President Biden attended

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:33.011 line:0%
the 99th annual National
Christmas Tree Lighting.

00:13:33.011 --> 00:13:35.447 line:0%
Meanwhile the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree was like,

00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:39.751
"Uh, yeah, sure, that's
the national Christmas tree."

00:13:39.751 --> 00:13:41.187
And this was special.

00:13:41.187 --> 00:13:43.988
A real-life Elf on the Shelf
made an appearance.

00:13:43.988 --> 00:13:45.558
Yeah, he got up and said,

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:48.226
"For the last time,
my name is Pete Buttigieg."

00:13:48.226 --> 00:13:51.096
[ Laughter ]

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:52.363
Then organizers said,

00:13:52.363 --> 00:13:54.065
"Sorry. Here's the real
Elf on the Shelf."

00:13:54.065 --> 00:13:56.368
And then he got up and said,
"I'm sorry. For the last time,

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:59.338
my name is Dr. Fauci."
This is terrible.

00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:01.840
Who's writing these?
That's right.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.241
By all accounts,
it was a great time.

00:14:03.241 --> 00:14:04.543
I mean, it definitely
went better

00:14:04.543 --> 00:14:06.711
than Boris Johnson's
tree lighting in the U.K.

00:14:06.711 --> 00:14:08.046
This is real. Look at this.

00:14:08.046 --> 00:14:13.017
-Five, four, three, two, one!

00:14:13.017 --> 00:14:15.554
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:15.554 --> 00:14:16.988
[ Laughter ]

00:14:16.988 --> 00:14:19.124
-Aww.

00:14:19.124 --> 00:14:20.993
[ Laughter ]

00:14:20.993 --> 00:14:23.261
-"Yea-- Ohh.
All right. Go home, everybody."

00:14:23.261 --> 00:14:24.729
[ Laughter ]

00:14:24.729 --> 00:14:26.732
Let's get to some news.

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:29.368 line:0%
Earlier today, President Biden
revealed his plan to fight COVID

00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:32.137 line:0%
this winter, which includes
free at-home testing,

00:14:32.137 --> 00:14:35.874 line:0%
a public education campaign,
and no lockdowns.

00:14:35.874 --> 00:14:37.509
And everyone was like,
"Let's not rule out

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:38.910
day drinking so fast."

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:42.080
I mean, that's --

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.581
That's right. No lockdowns.

00:14:43.581 --> 00:14:44.783
Biden must have felt the glare

00:14:44.783 --> 00:14:46.685
of a million brides
planning their wedding.

00:14:46.685 --> 00:14:50.489
Like, "Don't you dare.
Don't you dare."

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:52.558
Biden's plan
also extends the mandate

00:14:52.558 --> 00:14:56.028
requiring people to wear masks
on public transit.

00:14:56.028 --> 00:14:58.196
Then people riding the New
York City subway here were like,

00:14:58.196 --> 00:15:00.699
"Yeah, can you also require
a mandate to wear pants?

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:02.701
Because masks are, like,

00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:05.637
eighth on the list
of what's happening here."

00:15:05.637 --> 00:15:08.106
[ Applause ]

00:15:08.106 --> 00:15:10.508
"Ohh! Applesauce."

00:15:10.508 --> 00:15:12.310
-"Don't grab the pole!"

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:15.514
[ Laughter ]

00:15:15.647 --> 00:15:17.549
-But Biden did lay out
an ambitious goal.

00:15:17.549 --> 00:15:19.617
By springtime, he wants
the majority of Americans

00:15:19.617 --> 00:15:22.154
to know
how to pronounce "omicron."

00:15:22.154 --> 00:15:23.721 line:0%
-It's called the omnicron.

00:15:23.721 --> 00:15:26.992 line:0%
Omnicron. Omnicron.
The omnicron variant.

00:15:26.992 --> 00:15:29.160
[ Laughter ]

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.997
-Ombicrombie and Fitch.

00:15:31.997 --> 00:15:34.232
I read that President Trump

00:15:34.232 --> 00:15:36.167
might have tried
to self-publish his memoir

00:15:36.167 --> 00:15:38.303
to avoid getting
a smaller advance

00:15:38.303 --> 00:15:40.405
than President Obama
got for his memoir.

00:15:40.405 --> 00:15:42.274
Yeah, and Trump
is even considering

00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:44.043
a few titles for his book.

00:15:44.043 --> 00:15:45.311
For example...

00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:47.846
-Oh, here we go.

00:15:47.846 --> 00:15:50.348
-What's up, Mark?
-Let me guess.

00:15:50.348 --> 00:15:51.716
You're gonna make fun of Trump

00:15:51.716 --> 00:15:54.086
by saying a bunch
of fake book titles.

00:15:54.086 --> 00:15:56.688
-I mean, yeah,
that was the plan.

00:15:56.688 --> 00:15:58.156
-Oh, let me guess.

00:15:58.156 --> 00:16:00.191
And then each cover
will pop up on the screen,

00:16:00.191 --> 00:16:03.027
and people will see it
and laugh about it.

00:16:03.027 --> 00:16:04.663
-Right. We often show graphics

00:16:04.663 --> 00:16:06.364
during the monologue
to make our audience laugh.

00:16:06.364 --> 00:16:09.001
-Man, I know exactly
how this will go down.

00:16:09.001 --> 00:16:12.203
You'll start off with something
like, "Tweet Pray Love."

00:16:12.203 --> 00:16:13.973
-Yeah.
-Yeah, then you'll

00:16:13.973 --> 00:16:17.775
follow it up with,
"Oh, the Places You'll Riot!"

00:16:17.775 --> 00:16:20.412
-Yeah, then you'll do,
"Are You There Vlad?

00:16:20.412 --> 00:16:22.414
It's me, Donald."
-Yeah.

00:16:22.414 --> 00:16:23.882
-Oh, oh, and after that,

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:26.785
you're gonna do,
"Fifty Shades of COVID."

00:16:26.785 --> 00:16:29.454
-Yep. Yeah, these are all
pretty good examples. Yeah.

00:16:29.454 --> 00:16:30.989
-Oh, and then you'll do one

00:16:30.989 --> 00:16:33.892
that says,
"Lord of the Onion Rings."

00:16:33.892 --> 00:16:35.093
-Wait, wait. No, no.

00:16:35.093 --> 00:16:38.497
You'll do, "From Whom
the Taco Bell Tolls."

00:16:38.497 --> 00:16:40.165
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:16:40.165 --> 00:16:42.067
And then instead of "Clifford
the Big Red Dog," you'll do,

00:16:42.067 --> 00:16:43.935
"Clip-On the Big Red Tie."
-Yeah, I know.

00:16:43.935 --> 00:16:46.204
But these are -- We probably
wouldn't do this many.

00:16:46.204 --> 00:16:48.040
But, yeah,
these are all great examples.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.274
-Oh, then you'll do,

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:51.910
"Nineteen Eighty
Four Seasons Total Landscaping."

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.245
-Yeah, exactly.
-Or a couple where you don't

00:16:54.245 --> 00:16:56.314
